content.text:
PR is open: https://github.com/Vaibhaav-Tiwari/neatlogs-hack/pull/24

I did not run FDJ-1. The blocker is the proof step: `fly-doom-jev-9` ran `git status` without a prompt, but its Claude transcript still records `permissionMode: "default"`, not `auto`. Since the instruction was to prove transcript auto mode before spending on the task, I stopped there and reported it to the orchestrator.

Applied `fly-doom-jev` config change:

```json
// before
{
  "agentConfig": { "permissions": "auto" },
  "worker": { "agent": "claude-code", "agentConfig": {} }
}

// after
{
  "agentConfig": { "permissions": "auto" },
  "worker": { "agent": "claude-code", "agentConfig": { "permissions": "auto" } }
}
```

Code changes in PR #24:
- Real-run preflight now fails before spawn unless the target AO project has worker-scoped `permissions: "auto"`.
- `tally doctor --config ...` reports AO worker auto mode with the exact `ao project set-config ... --config-json ...` fix command.
- Fixed the flaky Neatlogs dry-run unit path by avoiding eager construction of real adapters when fake ports are supplied.

Verified:
- `npm test` passed: 196 tests
- `npm run typecheck` passed
- `npm run build` passed
- `tally doctor` for the FDJ config reports all connected
- `tally run --plan --only FDJ-1 --budget 1.50` routes FDJ-1 to `claude-code/claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` with `$0.80` ceiling.

